            "review_title": "Review at Ngo 89",
            "review_text": "David F\n4 contributions\n0\nLoved this place!!\nSep 2018 • Business\nI just happened upon this restaurant and liked the vibe and had my first meal not knowing what I was ordering or what sub-specialty of Vietnamese food it was. I was very happily surprised to find it some of the best food I ever had. It is apparently \"street food\" from the Hanoi region. The soup on the top left of the menu (see photo) is probably the tastiest soup I have ever had in my life. They call it \"Hanoi Traditional Cake\" but it looked and tasted like soup to me. I went back every day for it. The wraps and rolls are great as well. The chairs are half-normal height - this appears to be a signal that it's \"street food\" - so not the most comfortable in the world but the food makes up for it. \n\nI was telling an Aussie at my hotel about the place and he said, \"No way I'm eating street food, mate! I'm not spending my vacation crouched over the toilet\". I told him I'd been eating at the place every day, am likewise a weak-stomached Westerner, and didn't have any problems. He refused to believe me. I hope you will, at least if you're looking for the tastiest food I had anywhere in Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 12, 2018",
