            "review_text": "mriwa\nOslo, Norway20 contributions\n0\nRidiculously small portions, rude manager\nJan 2018 • Family\nThe place looks nice from the outside, and it has an attractive menu - \"authentic\" North Vietnamese streetfood, or so it seems. Alas, the first impression is misleading, and so is the menu. We ordered the grilled fish with noodles (a famous Hanoian dish); the picture on the menu promised us a decent portion, with about 12 pieces of fish. Sadly, what we got was a small dish with 6 tiny pieces of fish, not even fresh, which nearly drowned in the dill and spring onion. When we mentioned this to the manager, he reacted rudely, saying he could cut the pieces in two if we wanted. Later, when we paid the bill (overpriced, considering both quantity and quality), he \"forgot\" to give us our 40,000 dong change. A place best avoided!\nRead more\nWritten January 5, 2018",
